# Title: Potentially Suspicious File Download From ZIP TLD
# ID: 0bb4bbeb-fe52-4044-b40c-430a04577ebe
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2023-05-18
# Tags: attack.stealth
# Description: Detects the download of a file with a potentially suspicious extension from a .zip top level domain.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(Contents CONTAIN ".zip/" AND (TargetFilename CONTAIN ".bat:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".dat:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".dll:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".doc:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".docm:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".exe:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".hta:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".pptm:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".ps1:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".rar:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".rtf:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".sct:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".vbe:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".vbs:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".ws:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".wsf:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".xll:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".xls:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".xlsm:Zone" OR TargetFilename CONTAIN ".zip:Zone"))
